        "v": 5,
        "title": "Remove noisy debug logs in spawn-agents handler",
        "summary": "Removed `logger.debug` calls for subagent cost aggregation and parent agent total cost updates in `backend/src/tools/handlers/tool/spawn-agents.ts`. These frequent logs had narrow debugging value. Internal refactor only; no behavior change.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T10:06:20.339Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When an assistant works with other helper assistants, it quietly tracks how much each one costs so it can bill you correctly. The system used to write a line in the log file every time it added up one of those costs, and now it doesn't. If you were watching the internal logs, you'd see the \"Aggregating successful subagent cost\" and \"Updated parent agent total cost\" entries are gone, while the actual cost totals are still calculated exactly the same way.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
