      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Validate agent subagents against local and database sources",
        "summary": "Agent validation now checks spawnable agents against both locally defined templates and published agents in the database. `validateSpawnableAgents` was made async and `fetchAgent` was added to query the database for missing agent IDs. The `agent-registry` no longer skips subagent validation, and the `/publish` and `/validate` web APIs use the new `validateAgentsWithSpawnableAgents` function.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T10:06:42.159Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you or the system asks whether a listed helper-agent actually exists and can be used, the system now checks in two places instead of one: your locally defined agents and the published agents stored in the database. Any helper-agent reference that cannot be found in either source is now flagged as a validation error, so publishing or validating a set of agents will fail if a referenced subagent is missing from both sources. You would notice this if you try to publish or validate agents through the web interface and a referenced subagent no longer turns a blind eye, it now produces a concrete error instead of being silently allowed.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "11fe20c67470",
